# Copy to .env.local for development, and add the same keys in your host's
# dashboard for production. All are optional — the site builds and runs
# without them, it just degrades gracefully.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Public site URL
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The canonical domain is now baked in: https://shxzd.dev (see
# src/lib/site-url.ts). Production builds use it automatically, so LEAVE THIS
# BLANK unless you are moving the site to a different domain.
#
# It matters twice over. Link previews (the card X, Telegram and LinkedIn
# show) need an ABSOLUTE image URL — get it wrong and the preview silently
# disappears. And the canonical tag needs the real hostname, or Google indexes
# the wrong one and the site does not rank for your name. No trailing slash.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Search Console verification
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Only needed for the "HTML tag" verification method. Add the property at
# <https://search.google.com/search-console>, choose HTML tag, and paste ONLY
# the content="..." value here — not the whole <meta> tag.
#
# Left blank, no verification tag is emitted at all. That is deliberate: an
# empty content="" can fail the check outright rather than being ignored.
#
# If you verify by DNS record instead (the better option — it covers every
# subdomain and survives redeploys) you never need this.
GOOGLE_SITE_VERIFICATION=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GitHub contribution graph
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Without this the Signal section shows a seeded placeholder grid and labels
# itself "sample data". With it, the graph is your real contribution calendar.
#
# GitHub's REST API does not expose the contribution calendar; only GraphQL
# does, and it requires auth even for public data. Hence the token.
#
# Create one at https://github.com/settings/tokens
#   Classic token  -> tick the `read:user` scope, nothing else.
#   Fine-grained   -> read-only access to your own profile is enough.
# Never commit the real value.
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Contact form email
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Without this, /api/contact still validates and rate-limits, but only logs the
# message to the server console. See the TODO in src/app/api/contact/route.ts.
RESEND_API_KEY=
